From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:44:11 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 24/42] Plutonium: Google sign-in on the web; tabs fullscreen
 outside the shells

EXO-SIGNIN: in shell mode Mirror account consistency is off. Under Mirror,
Gaia answered a sign-in page with X-Chrome-Manage-Accounts and Chrome
cancelled the navigation for the OS "Add account" dialog, which Plutonium
doesn't have: "Sign in" on YouTube or Gmail did nothing. Google sign-in is
now the web's, as in any other browser, and no reconcilor touches the
cookies.

EXO-PRESENT for tabs: the switcher opens a tab fullscreen on its own, in
front of the shells, as it does windows. It is the tab's own page (its
state, input and focus), not its URL loaded again.
- PlutoniumTabs::Present/EndPresentation, and TabInfo.presented. The tab
  is detached from its <embed>, which keeps wanting it; a new
  SurfaceEmbedHost child filter keeps every <embed> from taking it back
  until the presentation ends, when the visible shell's does.
- PlutoniumTabPresenter (Ash) shows it in a fullscreen window with a
  views::WebView.
- The switcher: a tab's left click (and Enter) opens it fullscreen; its
  page has Open/Leave fullscreen, Show in its shell, and loading its
  address in the backup browser. Super+F or showing a shell ends it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
